WEBVTT

00:00.590 --> 00:04.640
Determine whether the
ordered pairs 3 comma 5 and 1

00:04.640 --> 00:09.740
comma negative 7 are solutions
to the inequality 5x minus 3y

00:09.740 --> 00:14.040
is greater than or equal to 25.

00:14.040 --> 00:17.060
So again, let me just try
each of these ordered pairs.

00:17.060 --> 00:19.290
We could try what happens
when x is equal to 3

00:19.290 --> 00:21.720
and y is equal to 5
in this inequality

00:21.720 --> 00:23.314
and see if it satisfies it.

00:23.314 --> 00:25.230
And then we could try
it for 1 and negative 7.

00:25.230 --> 00:27.220
So let's do that first.

00:27.220 --> 00:29.750
Let's do it first for 3 and 5.

00:29.750 --> 00:31.970
So when x is 3, y is 5.

00:31.970 --> 00:34.410
Let's see if this
actually gets satisfied.

00:34.410 --> 00:39.176
So we get 5 times 3.

00:39.176 --> 00:40.050
Let me color code it.

00:40.050 --> 00:45.070
So this is 5-- I didn't want to
do it in that color-- 5 times

00:45.070 --> 00:52.200
3 minus 3 times 5.

00:56.380 --> 01:02.640
Let's see if this is
greater than or equal to 25.

01:02.640 --> 01:05.900
So 5 times 3 is 15.

01:05.900 --> 01:09.350
And then from that, we're
going to subtract 15,

01:09.350 --> 01:12.915
and let's see if that is
greater than or equal to 25.

01:12.915 --> 01:15.150
Put that question mark
there because we don't know.

01:15.150 --> 01:17.700
And 15 minus 15, that is 0.

01:17.700 --> 01:22.810
So we get the expression 0 is
greater than or equal to 25.

01:22.810 --> 01:23.970
This is not true.

01:23.970 --> 01:26.640
0 is less than 25.

01:26.640 --> 01:28.580
So this is not true.

01:28.580 --> 01:30.130
This is not true.

01:30.130 --> 01:35.030
So this ordered pair is not
a solution to the inequality.

01:35.030 --> 01:39.450
So this is not a solution.

01:39.450 --> 01:41.810
You put in x is
3, y is 5, you get

01:41.810 --> 01:43.840
0 is greater than
or equal to 25,

01:43.840 --> 01:46.360
which is absolutely not true.

01:46.360 --> 01:49.390
Now let's try it with
1 and negative 7.

01:49.390 --> 02:00.140
So we have 5 times 1
minus 3 times negative 7

02:00.140 --> 02:03.120
needs to be greater
than or equal to 25.

02:03.120 --> 02:07.120
5 times 1 is 5, and then
minus 3 times negative 7

02:07.120 --> 02:08.229
is negative 21.

02:08.229 --> 02:11.295
So it becomes minus
negative 21 is

02:11.295 --> 02:13.610
to be greater than
or equal to 25.

02:13.610 --> 02:17.300
This is the same thing as
5 plus 21-- subtracting

02:17.300 --> 02:20.170
a negative same thing as
adding the positive-- is

02:20.170 --> 02:22.520
greater than or equal to 25.

02:22.520 --> 02:29.510
And 5 plus 21 is 26 is indeed
greater than or equal to 25.

02:29.510 --> 02:30.770
So this works out.

02:30.770 --> 02:33.512
So this is a solution.

02:33.512 --> 02:34.970
And just to see if
we can visualize

02:34.970 --> 02:38.287
this a little bit better, I'm
going to graph this inequality.

02:38.287 --> 02:40.620
I'm not going to show you
exactly how I do it this time,

02:40.620 --> 02:43.280
but I'm going to show you
where these points lie relative

02:43.280 --> 02:44.055
to this solution.

02:47.420 --> 02:50.750
So we have 5-- let me
do this is a new color.

02:50.750 --> 02:55.830
So we have 5x-- that's
not a new color.

02:55.830 --> 02:57.530
Having trouble
switching colors today.

02:57.530 --> 03:04.090
We have 5x minus 3y is
greater than or equal to 25.

03:04.090 --> 03:05.590
Let me write this
inequality in kind

03:05.590 --> 03:06.927
of our slope-intercept form.

03:06.927 --> 03:08.260
So this would be the same thing.

03:08.260 --> 03:10.830
If we subtract 5x
from both sides,

03:10.830 --> 03:14.020
we get negative
3y is greater than

03:14.020 --> 03:18.510
or equal to negative 5x plus 25.

03:18.510 --> 03:20.420
I just subtracted
5x from both sides.

03:20.420 --> 03:23.850
So that gets eliminated, and you
have a negative 5x over here.

03:23.850 --> 03:26.210
Now let's divide both
sides of this equation,

03:26.210 --> 03:29.182
or I should say this
inequality, by negative 3.

03:29.182 --> 03:31.140
And when you divide both
sides of an inequality

03:31.140 --> 03:33.730
by a negative number, multiply
or divide by a negative number,

03:33.730 --> 03:35.580
it swaps the inequality.

03:35.580 --> 03:37.360
So if you divide both
sides by negative 3,

03:37.360 --> 03:42.920
you get y is less than or
equal to negative 5 divided

03:42.920 --> 03:46.560
by negative 3 is 5 over 3x.

03:46.560 --> 03:51.370
And then 25 divided by
negative 3 is minus 25/3.

03:55.190 --> 03:57.860
So this is now the
expression or the inequality,

03:57.860 --> 04:03.850
y is less than or equal
to 5/3 x minus 25/3.

04:03.850 --> 04:05.930
So if I wanted to
graph this-- I'll

04:05.930 --> 04:08.224
try to draw a relatively
rough graph here,

04:08.224 --> 04:10.140
but really just so that
we can visualize this.

04:14.420 --> 04:17.740
So our y-intercept
is negative 25/3.

04:17.740 --> 04:20.380
That's the same thing
as negative 8 and 1/3.

04:20.380 --> 04:24.240
So that's 1, 2,
3, 4, 5, 6, 7, 8,

04:24.240 --> 04:25.650
and a little bit more than 8.

04:25.650 --> 04:30.120
So our y-intercept is
negative 8 and 1/3 like that.

04:30.120 --> 04:32.860
And it has a slope of 5/3.

04:32.860 --> 04:36.320
So that means for every 3 it
goes to the right, it rises 5.

04:36.320 --> 04:41.120
So it goes 1, 2, 3, it rises 5.

04:41.120 --> 04:43.515
So the line is going to
look something like this.

04:43.515 --> 04:45.590
I'm drawing a very
rough version of it.

04:45.590 --> 04:49.950
So the line will look something
like that, this line over here.

04:49.950 --> 04:55.480
That's if it was a y is
equal to 5/3 x minus 25/3.

04:55.480 --> 04:56.810
But here we have an inequality.

04:56.810 --> 04:59.740
It's y is less than or equal to.

04:59.740 --> 05:04.490
So for any x, the y's that
satisfy it are the y's

05:04.490 --> 05:09.550
that equals 5/3 x minus 25/3--
that would be on the line,

05:09.550 --> 05:10.970
so it would be
that point there--

05:10.970 --> 05:12.820
and all the y's less than it.

05:12.820 --> 05:16.360
So the solution is this
whole area right over here.

05:16.360 --> 05:20.160
Since it's less than or equal
to, we can include the line.

05:20.160 --> 05:22.360
The equal to allows us
to include the line,

05:22.360 --> 05:25.260
and the less than tells us we're
going to go below the line.

05:25.260 --> 05:26.931
And we can verify
that by looking

05:26.931 --> 05:28.180
at these two points over here.

05:28.180 --> 05:31.870
We saw that 3 comma 5 is
not part of the solution.

05:31.870 --> 05:35.010
So 3 comma 5 is 1, 2--
it's right about there

05:35.010 --> 05:35.760
and then up 5.

05:35.760 --> 05:39.252
So 3 comma 5 is
right above here.

05:39.252 --> 05:40.710
It's in this region
above the line,

05:40.710 --> 05:42.590
and notice not part
of the solution.

05:42.590 --> 05:48.610
And then 1 comma negative 7 is
going to be right over here.

05:48.610 --> 05:50.020
It's almost on the line.

05:50.020 --> 05:54.630
So 1 comma negative 7 is
going to be right over there.

05:54.630 --> 05:58.016
But it is, at least,
within this solution area.

05:58.016 --> 06:00.140
So hopefully that gives
you a little bit more sense

06:00.140 --> 06:01.514
of how to visualize
these things.

06:01.514 --> 06:05.200
And we'll cover this in more
detail in future videos.
